  "releaseNotes": "HttpModel Header Management Enhancements:\n      - Added 'AllocHeaderOption' (Default: false) to HttpModel for high-performance builder scenarios.\n      - Optimized Header/Cookie indexing: Zero-allocation by default. Memory for Map indexing (ByteString) is only consumed if explicitly enabled or during lazy lookup.\n      - Improved 'AddHeader' and 'SetHeader' logic to ensure data consistency even when a Body is not yet present.\n      - Enhanced memory safety: Internal cache map now uses internal buffer Spans to prevent \"Stale Pointer\" issues during buffer resizing.\n      - Support for Lazy Loading headers: Fetching headers by index will automatically populate the generic lookup cache.\n      - Internal refactoring of Utf8Map for better case-insensitive comparison performance.\n      - Fixed a bug where headers were not indexed during manual building if no body was set.",
